import{_ as e,o as i,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"The Symbiotic Education System","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/37-共生教育体系.md","filePath":"en/37-共生教育体系.md","lastUpdated":null}'),a={name:"en/37-共生教育体系.md"};function r(l,t,s,c,d,u){return i(),o("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[n('<h1 id="the-symbiotic-education-system" tabindex="-1">The Symbiotic Education System <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-symbiotic-education-system" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Symbiotic Education System&quot;">​</a></h1><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Document No.</td><td>37</td></tr><tr><td>Module</td><td>Civilization Typologies and Social Systems</td></tr><tr><td>Keywords</td><td>Symbiotic Education, Lifelong Learning, Open Systems, Teaching According to Aptitude, Educational Equity</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="i-core-concepts-and-goals-of-symbiotic-education" tabindex="-1">I. Core Concepts and Goals of Symbiotic Education <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-core-concepts-and-goals-of-symbiotic-education" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Core Concepts and Goals of Symbiotic Education&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Education is the cornerstone of civilizational inheritance and development. In the era of the Predatory Cultivation System, education was monopolized by a few powerhouses and sects, and the masses at the bottom had almost no opportunity to receive formal education. This educational monopoly not only caused class solidification, but also led to the low efficiency of the overall evolution of civilization — the potential of most lives was wasted, while a few monopolists deliberately restricted the spread of knowledge and innovation in order to protect their privileges.</p><p>After the establishment of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, building an open, fair, and high-quality symbiotic education system became one of its core tasks. The core concept of symbiotic education can be summarized in sixteen characters: &quot;A Path for Everyone, Teaching According to Aptitude, Lifelong Learning, Myriad Races Advancing Together.&quot;</p><p>The core goals of symbiotic education include:</p><ol><li><strong>Universal basic cultivation education</strong>: ensure that every symbiotic life can acquire basic cultivation knowledge and ability, realizing &quot;A Path for Everyone&quot;</li><li><strong>Cultivating high-end cultivation talents</strong>: through advanced education and elite education, cultivate high-end talents in various fields, providing intellectual support for civilizational development</li><li><strong>Promoting the all-round development of individuals</strong>: not only cultivating cultivation ability, but also focusing on the cultivation of comprehensive qualities such as morality, wisdom, creativity, and social responsibility</li><li><strong>Promoting civilizational inheritance and innovation</strong>: realize the intergenerational inheritance of civilization through education, while stimulating innovative vitality and promoting continuous civilizational progress</li><li><strong>Serving the advancement of the Myriad Races</strong>: the education system is open to all races and life forms, promoting exchange and common progress among the Myriad Races</li></ol><h2 id="ii-the-four-level-system-of-symbiotic-education" tabindex="-1">II. The Four-Level System of Symbiotic Education <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-four-level-system-of-symbiotic-education" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Four-Level System of Symbiotic Education&quot;">​</a></h2><p>According to the educational stage and cultivation goals, the symbiotic education system is divided into four levels, forming a complete educational chain:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Level</th><th>Name</th><th>Target Students</th><th>Core Goals</th><th>Duration</th><th>Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>First Level</td><td>Enlightenment Education</td><td>All underage lives</td><td>Basic knowledge, cultivation introduction, moral enlightenment</td><td>6-9 years</td><td>Free</td></tr><tr><td>Second Level</td><td>Basic Education</td><td>Those who completed enlightenment education</td><td>Systematic cultivation knowledge, basic cultivation ability, comprehensive qualities</td><td>3-6 years</td><td>Free</td></tr><tr><td>Third Level</td><td>Advanced Education</td><td>Those who passed the basic assessment</td><td>Professional cultivation skills, in-depth system research, innovation ability</td><td>3-9 years</td><td>Low fee/scholarships</td></tr><tr><td>Fourth Level</td><td>Elite Education</td><td>Selected high-potential individuals</td><td>Top cultivation realms, law research, civilizational leadership ability</td><td>No limit</td><td>Fully funded</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="_2-1-enlightenment-education" tabindex="-1">2.1 Enlightenment Education <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-1-enlightenment-education" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.1 Enlightenment Education&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Enlightenment education is the starting point of the symbiotic education system, open to all underage lives and completely free. Its core content includes:</p><ul><li><strong>Basic knowledge</strong>: language and writing, mathematical logic, cosmic common knowledge, civilizational history, and other basic knowledge</li><li><strong>Cultivation introduction</strong>: basic introduction to the Three Hundred Origin Cultivation Systems, basic breathing techniques, energy perception training, etc.</li><li><strong>Moral enlightenment</strong>: cultivation of symbiotic concepts, ethics and morality, social responsibility, and the value of equality among the Myriad Races</li><li><strong>Interest discovery</strong>: through diversified courses and activities, help every child discover their own interests and strengths</li></ul><p>Enlightenment education emphasizes &quot;happy learning, all-round development.&quot; It does not engage in fierce competition or screening, but focuses on protecting children&#39;s curiosity and creativity.</p><h3 id="_2-2-basic-education" tabindex="-1">2.2 Basic Education <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-2-basic-education" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.2 Basic Education&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Basic education is oriented toward adolescents who have completed enlightenment education and is also completely free. Its core content includes:</p><ul><li><strong>Systematic cultivation knowledge</strong>: systematic study and understanding of the Three Hundred Origin Cultivation Systems</li><li><strong>Basic cultivation ability</strong>: master at least one basic cultivation system, reaching the level of an initial cultivator</li><li><strong>Comprehensive quality cultivation</strong>: all-round cultivation of scientific literacy, humanistic literacy, artistic literacy, and physical fitness</li><li><strong>Social practice</strong>: through community service, practical activities, etc., cultivate social responsibility and practical ability</li></ul><p>At the end of the basic education stage, students must take a basic assessment. Those who pass may enter advanced education; those who fail may choose to retake it, or directly enter society to engage in basic work.</p><h3 id="_2-3-advanced-education" tabindex="-1">2.3 Advanced Education <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-3-advanced-education" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.3 Advanced Education&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Advanced education is oriented toward cultivators who passed the basic assessment, operating through a combination of low fees and scholarships. Its core content includes:</p><ul><li><strong>Professional cultivation directions</strong>: students choose their major cultivation systems and professional directions for in-depth study</li><li><strong>Practical cultivation training</strong>: under the guidance of mentors, engage in extensive practical cultivation to improve actual ability</li><li><strong>Technology R&amp;D capability</strong>: cultivate research and development capability in cultivation technology and engineering technology</li><li><strong>Professional quality cultivation</strong>: cultivate professional ethics, teamwork, communication and expression, and other professional qualities</li></ul><p>Advanced education is divided into multiple professional directions, covering cultivation, technology, management, education, medicine, arts, and other fields. Students can choose their professional direction according to their interests and strengths.</p><h3 id="_2-4-elite-education" tabindex="-1">2.4 Elite Education <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-4-elite-education" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2.4 Elite Education&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Elite education is oriented toward high-potential cultivators selected through strict screening, fully funded by the symbiotic civilization. Its core content includes:</p><ul><li><strong>Top cultivation guidance</strong>: one-on-one guidance by mentors at the Plane-Supreme Powerhouse level</li><li><strong>In-depth law research</strong>: in-depth research on the Origin Laws of the universe, exploring the ultimate mysteries of cultivation</li><li><strong>Civilizational leadership ability</strong>: cultivate strategic thinking, governance ability, innovation ability, and other qualities necessary for civilizational leaders</li><li><strong>Cross-Plane vision</strong>: through cross-plane exchange and exploration, cultivate a universe-level vision and pattern</li></ul><p>The goal of elite education is to cultivate the future leaders of the symbiotic civilization, so the selection is extremely strict and the training resources are extremely abundant.</p><h2 id="iii-core-principles-of-symbiotic-education" tabindex="-1">III. Core Principles of Symbiotic Education <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-core-principles-of-symbiotic-education" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Core Principles of Symbiotic Education&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_3-1-the-principle-of-educational-equity" tabindex="-1">3.1 The Principle of Educational Equity <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-1-the-principle-of-educational-equity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.1 The Principle of Educational Equity&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Educational equity is the primary principle of symbiotic education. The symbiotic civilization guarantees educational equity through the following measures:</p><ul><li><strong>Free basic education</strong>: enlightenment education and basic education are completely free, ensuring that every child can attend school</li><li><strong>Balanced educational resources</strong>: through the Anchor Network, realize remote sharing of high-quality educational resources, narrowing regional gaps</li><li><strong>Compensation for disadvantaged groups</strong>: provide additional educational support for poor families, special races, disabled lives, and other disadvantaged groups</li><li><strong>Unified selection standards</strong>: the selection for advanced and elite education uses ability and potential as the sole criteria, without regard to origin or wealth</li></ul><h3 id="_3-2-the-principle-of-teaching-according-to-aptitude" tabindex="-1">3.2 The Principle of Teaching According to Aptitude <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-2-the-principle-of-teaching-according-to-aptitude" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.2 The Principle of Teaching According to Aptitude&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Symbiotic education emphasizes teaching according to aptitude, respecting the differences of each individual:</p><ul><li><strong>Personalized assessment</strong>: every student receives a comprehensive personality assessment upon enrollment, including talent, interests, traits, learning styles, etc.</li><li><strong>Personalized learning plans</strong>: based on assessment results, formulate personalized learning plans for each student</li><li><strong>Diversified course options</strong>: provide a rich variety of courses for students to choose from, meeting different interests and development directions</li><li><strong>Flexible learning pace</strong>: allow students to adjust their learning pace according to their own circumstances; fast learners can skip grades, slow learners can extend their study time</li></ul><h3 id="_3-3-the-principle-of-lifelong-learning" tabindex="-1">3.3 The Principle of Lifelong Learning <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-3-the-principle-of-lifelong-learning" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.3 The Principle of Lifelong Learning&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Symbiotic education is not limited to the underage stage, but runs through the entire life of each individual:</p><ul><li><strong>Adult continuing education</strong>: provide adults with opportunities for continuous learning and skill improvement</li><li><strong>Job-transition training</strong>: provide training support for individuals who need to change cultivation directions or careers</li><li><strong>Elderly learning</strong>: provide learning opportunities for elderly cultivators in health preservation, culture, interests, etc.</li><li><strong>Online learning platforms</strong>: provide abundant online learning resources through the symbiotic network, allowing learning anytime and anywhere</li></ul><h3 id="_3-4-the-principle-of-practice-orientation" tabindex="-1">3.4 The Principle of Practice Orientation <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-4-the-principle-of-practice-orientation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3.4 The Principle of Practice Orientation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Symbiotic education emphasizes the combination of theory and practice:</p><ul><li><strong>Practical cultivation</strong>: students engage in extensive practical cultivation while learning theory</li><li><strong>Internship and practical training</strong>: the advanced education stage arranges extensive internships and practical training, allowing students to train in real environments</li><li><strong>Project-driven learning</strong>: driven by actual projects, cultivating students&#39; ability to solve real problems</li><li><strong>School-enterprise cooperation</strong>: educational institutions cooperate closely with cultivation institutions and enterprises to jointly cultivate talents</li></ul><h2 id="iv-faculty-and-resource-guarantees-for-symbiotic-education" tabindex="-1">IV. Faculty and Resource Guarantees for Symbiotic Education <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-faculty-and-resource-guarantees-for-symbiotic-education" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Faculty and Resource Guarantees for Symbiotic Education&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_4-1-faculty-development" tabindex="-1">4.1 Faculty Development <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-1-faculty-development" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4.1 Faculty Development&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The symbiotic civilization has established a complete faculty training and management system:</p><ul><li><strong>Teacher qualification certification</strong>: all teachers must pass strict qualification certification to ensure teaching quality</li><li><strong>Continuous teacher training</strong>: teachers must participate in regular training to continuously update knowledge and improve teaching ability</li><li><strong>Mentor incentive mechanism</strong>: excellent mentors can receive honors, resource quotas, promotion opportunities, and other incentives</li><li><strong>Mentor obligation system</strong>: advanced cultivators have the obligation to serve as mentors and guide initial cultivators</li></ul><h3 id="_4-2-educational-resource-guarantees" tabindex="-1">4.2 Educational Resource Guarantees <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-2-educational-resource-guarantees" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4.2 Educational Resource Guarantees&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The symbiotic civilization guarantees an adequate supply of educational resources through various means:</p><ul><li><strong>Public financial investment</strong>: government finances give priority to educational investment; education expenditure must not be lower than the legally prescribed proportion of public expenditure</li><li><strong>Social forces in education</strong>: encourage sects, enterprises, non-profit organizations, and other social forces to participate in running schools</li><li><strong>Resource sharing mechanism</strong>: realize the sharing of high-quality educational resources across the whole domain through the Anchor Network</li><li><strong>Open educational resources</strong>: the basic techniques of the Three Hundred Origin Cultivation Systems are all opened free of charge as educational resources</li></ul><h3 id="_4-3-application-of-educational-technology" tabindex="-1">4.3 Application of Educational Technology <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-3-application-of-educational-technology" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4.3 Application of Educational Technology&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The symbiotic civilization makes full use of advanced technology to improve educational quality:</p><ul><li><strong>Remote teaching</strong>: realize cross-regional and cross-plane remote teaching through the Anchor Network</li><li><strong>Intelligent tutoring</strong>: use artificial intelligence technology to provide personalized intelligent tutoring for students</li><li><strong>Simulated cultivation</strong>: use virtual space technology to provide students with a safe simulated cultivation environment</li><li><strong>Data analysis</strong>: use big data analysis of students&#39; learning situations to provide precise teaching recommendations</li></ul><h2 id="v-differences-in-educational-models-of-the-five-civilization-types" tabindex="-1">V. Differences in Educational Models of the Five Civilization Types <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-differences-in-educational-models-of-the-five-civilization-types" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Differences in Educational Models of the Five Civilization Types&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The five symbiotic civilization types have their own characteristics in educational models:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Educational Model Features</th><th>Advantages</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>East Asian Intensive Type</td><td>Large-scale, standardized, strict assessment</td><td>High training efficiency, solid foundation</td></tr><tr><td>Nordic Welfare Type</td><td>Universal, personalized, low pressure</td><td>Strong sense of well-being, good creativity</td></tr><tr><td>North American Pluralistic Type</td><td>Independent choice, competitive selection, elite education</td><td>Strong innovation, many top talents</td></tr><tr><td>Continental European Social Type</td><td>Dual-track, school-enterprise cooperation, career-oriented</td><td>Strong practical ability, high employment fit</td></tr><tr><td>Developing Catch-up Type</td><td>Elite-led, rapid popularization, learning and borrowing</td><td>Fast popularization, strong breakthrough ability</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The various types can learn from each other and continuously optimize their own educational models.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The symbiotic education system is the &quot;talent incubator&quot; and &quot;civilizational inheritor&quot; of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization. Through the four-level education system, the four core principles, and complete faculty and resource guarantees, symbiotic education provides every symbiotic life with a complete growth path from enlightenment to elite, realizing the educational goals of &quot;A Path for Everyone, Teaching According to Aptitude, Lifelong Learning, Myriad Races Advancing Together.&quot; The popularization and high quality of education are the fundamental guarantees for the symbiotic civilization to continuously evolve and for the Myriad Races to advance together.</p><h2 id="related-documents" tabindex="-1">Related Documents <a class="header-anchor" href="#related-documents" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related Documents&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>43-教育保障法 (Education Guarantee Law)</li><li>36-社会结构与阶层流动 (Social Structure and Class Mobility)</li><li>10-三百套本源修炼体系总览 (Overview of the Three Hundred Origin Cultivation Systems)</li></ul>',57)])])}const p=e(a,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
